# iCloud sync duplicates
* 2.*
* 2

# Pre-publish drafts (release deliberately with cosigner credit per master pitch §4.3).
# Use `docs/*` not `docs/` so negation patterns can re-include specific files
# (git cannot un-ignore a file whose parent directory is fully excluded).
docs/*
# Exception: quickstart.md is public onboarding, not a draft.
!docs/quickstart.md
# Exception: the audit-trail page documents verify_chain and the six audit columns, which
# shipped in 0.7.0 and were documented nowhere a user looks. Re-included BY NAME: widening
# this to docs/** is how a private draft gets published, and leaving it out is how a README
# link 404s, which has already happened twice.
!docs/audit-trail.md
# Exception: FOUR spec docs ship, each re-included by name below. The rest of
# docs/spec/ (private governance/schema drafts) stays private — do NOT broaden
# this to docs/spec/** or those private drafts would be published.
!docs/spec/
docs/spec/*
# 2026-09-12: scope.md was authored 2026-07-12 as the canonical public answer to "what
# fivedrisk assesses and what it deliberately does not", README.md:36 has linked it ever
# since, and `docs/spec/*` above silently swallowed it, so that link has 404'd for every
# reader. Re-included by name, never by widening the glob.
!docs/spec/scope.md
!docs/spec/taxonomy.md
!docs/spec/deployment.md

# Calibration data stays private until the corresponding comparison report ships
benchmarks/aiid-reconstructions.yaml
